cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or analysis, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "inscriptions: mixture-corrected summed probability analysis of Latin inscriptions and Roman urban population"
abstract: >-
  Code, preregistered analysis, and figures for applying summed probability
  analysis (SPA) to the Latin Inscriptions of the Roman Empire (LIRE v3.0),
  with a Bayesian deconvolution-mixture model that separates editorial
  round-number dating convention from genuine temporal signal, and relates
  inscription production to Hanson urban-population estimates.
type: software
